  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n(15, 5, 375)\n\n(14, 3, 210)\n\n**Logic:** Third no. = [(First no.) × (Second no.) × 5]\n\n**(15, 5, 375) →**\n\n⇒ (15 × 5 × 5)\n\n⇒ (15 × 25) = 375\n\n**(14, 3, 210) →**\n\n⇒ (14 × 3 × 5)\n\n⇒ (14 × 15) = 210\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n**1.** (10, 12, 320) →\n\n⇒ (10 × 12 × 5)\n\n⇒ (10 × 60) = 600\n\n**2.** (17, 19, 920) →\n\n⇒ (17 × 19 × 5)\n\n⇒ (17 × 95) = 1615\n\n**3. **(14, 15, 780) →\n\n⇒ (14 × 15 × 5)\n\n⇒ (14 × 75) = 1050\n\n**4.** **(11, 16, 880) →**\n\n⇒ (11 × 16 × 5)\n\n⇒ (11 × 80) = **880**\n\nHere, **(11, 16, 880)** shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (4)\".",
